:"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Code works, but for some reason there's an annoying bug for people switching between touch and mouse:\n\nAny time you interact with the mouse, the next touch drag will still behave as if it were a real mouse.\n\nThis PR as-is improves the situation massively, but this is somewhat annoying. No idea if this is a blocking issue or not. Hopefully it's trivially fixable, although at a glance I'm not sure what's happening.","state":"DISMISSED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119507#pullrequestreview-4348338284","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119507","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119507#pullrequestreview-4348338284"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119507"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-22T19:20:17Z","commit_id":"d09a94a6d2f6250f51cff3f52636e6ac582d8dbe"},{"id":4349850162,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA0VyMg","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?u=f6c14ec512c7cd33f8d109f121e89b7e60e42f38&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested on my Android phone (Redmi Note 11, Android 13). This PR mostly works as expected, I can now drag files in the file system, but, as pointed out by deralmas, the next touch input still behaves as if it were a mouse and drag is enabled, but the next touch input that comes after that behaves as expected (no drag).\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bb1ed592-6048-4077-bcfe-5d4b17177525\r\n\r\n> To enable dragging with touch input, I still need to brainstorm a workflow that allows both dragging and touch scrolling to coexist. Normally, apps starts drag-n-drop on long press, but it's currently used to show the context menu. \r\n\r\nWould it make sense to start dragging on double tap?","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119507#pullrequestreview-4349850162","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119507","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119507#pullrequestreview-4349850162"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119507"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-23T05:32:50Z","commit_id":"d09a94a6d2f6250f51cff3f52636e6ac582d8dbe"},{"id":4353556358,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA33_hg","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Now works! Changes look fine, with just one nitpick and then it's good IMO.\n\nI have a feeling that, at one point or another, `drag_touching` was meant to handle all of this, and now got relegated to just whether the feature is on or off. This is all speculation though.\n\nI wanted to do a more consistent analysis of the above but I soon found out that it (and the whole acceleration logic) [comes from \"GODOT IS OPEN SOURCE\"](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/0b806ee0fc9097fa7bda7ac0109191c9c5e0a1ac/scene/gui/tree.cpp#L2361-L2405) so... The reason this looks so anachronistic is that it *is* and we should probably look into this separately xD","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119507#pullrequestreview-4353556358","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119507","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119507#pullrequestreview-4353556358"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119507"}},"submitted_at":"2026-05-24T23:15:59Z","commit_id":"7750bb453883b767321af153d98dd9e33c6c6e90"}]